WEBVTT

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.001
HarborVoice   operations   briefing.  

00:00:02.540 --> 00:00:03.120
This   is   a  

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:04.541
fictional   training   example.  

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:06.620
Shipment   HV   two  

00:00:06.620 --> 00:00:07.620
zero   four   eight  

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:08.460
has   a   recorded  

00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:09.880
customs   hold.   The  

00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:10.940
assistant   can   report  

00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:11.680
the   record   and  

00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:12.740
explain   the   published  

00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:14.440
procedure.   It   cannot  

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:15.281
remove   the   hold.  

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:16.460
If   a   customer  

00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:17.940
requests   help,   create  

00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:18.880
a   pending   review  

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:19.680
request   with   the  

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:20.900
exact   reference   and  

00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:22.021
a   concrete   reason.  

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:23.260
Check   the   tool  

00:00:23.260 --> 00:00:24.660
result   before   describing  

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:26.180
its   outcome.   Never  

00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:27.080
turn   a   proposed  

00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:27.920
action   into   a  

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:29.620
completed   one.   Before  

00:00:29.620 --> 00:00:31.140
demonstrating   the   system,  

00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:32.180
verify   the   knowledge  

00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:33.320
index,   test   the  

00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:34.440
failure   path   and  

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:35.480
confirm   the   account  

00:00:35.480 --> 00:00:37.300
budget.   Good   automation  

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:38.020
makes   the   next  

00:00:38.020 --> 00:00:39.040
decision   clearer.
